// D binding tests (extern(C) + link-time). Like Nim/Zig/Go-cgo/Rust, D compiles
// and links: d.test() compiles-and-runs each test file with `dmd -run`, with the
// binding's own module (src/servirtium/package.d) compiled in via d_source() and
// the engine .so linked via d_flag() (-L forwards to the linker) + rpath.
//
// The engine .so is taken from ../core/native — the compat copy core/.build.ae
// stages next to the source tree (the same path go's cgo LDFLAGS bake in) — a
// fixed relative path from this module dir, since dmd runs with cwd = d/.
//
// tests/playback_test.d replays the canonical tape (GET /ok -> 200 text/plain
// "ok-body") and asserts the body, a clean match, the diagnostics, and what D
// adds (scope(exit) shutdown, GC'd strings with no manual free, a thrown
// VcrException instead of a dead handle). Skipped by preflight when dmd is
// absent (prereq dmd).
import bldr
import d
import d (d_source, test_file, d_flag)
aeb(cap) {
    bldr.build() {
        prereq("dmd")
        dep("core/.build.ae")
        d.test() {
            d_flag("-Isrc")
            // Link the engine .so from its in-tree staged location + bake rpath
            // so the test binary finds it at run time (dmd forwards -L<x> to ld).
            d_flag("-L-L../core/native")
            d_flag("-L-lservirtium_vcr")
            d_flag("-L-rpath")
            d_flag("-L../core/native")
            d_source("src/servirtium/package.d")
            test_file("tests/playback_test.d")
        }
    }
}
